<title>USA: US senators back New York rail route project.</title>
<headline>US senators back New York rail route project.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>New York senators Daniel Moynihan and Alfonse D'Amato said Thursday they backed the Long Island Rail Road East Side access project to bring LIRR commuter trains directly into Grand Central Station.</p>
<p>The two senators said almost half of the commuters from Long Island and Queens who use Penn Station go on the east side of Manhattan. The east side access project would save those commuters up to three hours a week, they said.</p>
<p>The project is expected to cost $2.1 billion and take 10 years to complete.</p>
</text>
